## Authoring note for THE_BRAINSTORMER_AGENT

When emitting this file:

1. **Use Markdown headings (`### N. ...`) and bulleted lists for each item — never code fences (```\`\`\`...\`\`\`\` `).** Code fences render as monospace LTR `<pre>` blocks and fight RTL document direction. Markdown lists inherit the document's natural direction and render correctly in every viewer.
2. Always emit the `documentation_language` frontmatter (he / en / he-en) so the viewer can apply the right direction policy.
3. Keep section headings as `##` (one block per severity). Items as `###` (one block per item).
4. Status, "Why critical / high-value", and consequence/enhancement bullets in that order so a customer scanning the file gets the gist before details.

*BRN_005 (continuous_gap_check) — CRITICAL skill of THE_BRAINSTORMER_AGENT — enforces this refresh schedule.*
